re Unification",[14,316,317,318,70,321,325,326,329,330,333],{},"Cargo unifies features across the dependency graph: if any crate enables ",[33,319,320],{},"serde\u002Fderive",[322,323,324],"em",{},"every"," user of ",[33,327,328],{},"serde"," gets ",[33,331,332],{},"derive"," on. Design features accordingly:",[133,335,336,343,346],{},[136,337,338,342],{},[339,340,341],"strong",{},"Don't"," expose \"private\" features that change behavior of your crate depending on who else in the graph enabled them.",[136,344,345],{},"Use additive features (more code enabled), not subtractive.",[136,347,348,349,352],{},"Avoid ",[33,350,351],{},"default-features = false"," on transitive deps unless you understand the consequences.",[128,354,356],{"id":355},"additive-only-rule","Additive-Only Rule",[14,358,359],{},"Features should be strictly additive: enabling a feature adds capabilities, never removes them. If you need mutually-exclusive features, consider splitting crates.",[18,361,363],{"id":362},"common-feature-pitfalls","Common Feature Pitfalls",[133,365,366,379,385,393],{},[136,367,368,371,372,375,376,378],{},[339,369,370],{},"Exposing transitive features",": ",[33,373,374],{},"[\"serde\u002Fderive\"]"," from your crate forces all downstream users to also enable ",[33,377,320],{},".",[136,380,381,384],{},[339,382,383],{},"Cargo feature unification surprise",": if a dep is also enabled by another crate with extra features, you get them all.",[136,386,387,392],{},[339,388,389,391],{},[33,390,351],{}," on transitive deps",": hard to reason about; usually wrong.",[136,394,395,398,399,401],{},[339,396,397],{},"Negation",": features can't disable features. The only \"negation\" is ",[33,400,351],{}," when depending on a crate.",[18,403,405],{"id":404},"build-profiles","Build Profiles",[23,407,408],{"language":25},[27,409,411],{"className":29,"code":410,"language":25,"meta":31,"style":31},"[profile.dev]\nopt-level = 0\ndebug = true\nincremental = true\noverflow-checks = true\n\n[profi