") in CI for libraries with several optional features — it compiles every combination, catching a ",[33,1688,1689],{},"#[cfg(feature = \"a\")]"," block that silently depends on feature ",[33,1692,1693],{},"b"," without declaring it.",[136,1696,1697,371,1699,1701,1702,1704,1705,1707],{},[339,1698,1024],{},[33,1700,725],{}," plus ",[33,1703,716],{}," gives the best runtime performance but the slowest release build — reserve this combination for the final distributed binary, not for every CI run, since a \"profiling\" or \"dist\" custom profile inheriting from ",[33,1706,471],{}," can isolate the cost to only when you need it.",[136,1709,1710,1712,1713,1715,1716,1719],{},[339,1711,1677],{},": set ",[33,1714,1184],{}," on internal workspace-only crates from the start — it costs nothing and prevents an embarrassing accidental ",[33,1717,1718],{},"cargo publish"," of a crate never meant for crates.io.",[136,1721,1722,371,1724,1727,1728,1730],{},[339,1723,1668],{},[33,1725,1726],{},"cargo publish --dry-run"," catches missing metadata (license, description) and packaging issues without actually publishing — always run it before the real ",[33,1729,1718],{},", especially the first time for a new crate.",[136,1732,1733,1735,1736,1738],{},[339,1734,1677],{},": prefer ",[33,1737,140],{}," syntax over a bare optional dependency when you don't want the feature name to be implicitly tied to the dependency's crate name — it decouples your public feature-flag API from your internal dependency choices, so swapping the underlying crate later isn't a breaking change to your feature flags.",[18,1740,1742],{"id":1741},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[133,1744,1745,1762,1774,1785,1797,1806],{},[136,1746,1747,1750,1751,1754,1755,1757,1758,1761],{},[339,1748,1749],{},"Feature unification breaking builds",": if your crate's ",[33,1752,1753],{},"cfg(feature = \"x\")"," only makes sense with another crate's feature, you can't express that without ",[33,1756,197],{},"\u002F",[33,1759,1760],{},"?dep\u002Ffeat"," syntax.",[136,1763,1764,1769,1770,1773],{},[339,1765,1766,1767],{},"Optional dep without ",[33,1768,197],{}," creates an implicit feature of the same name; sometimes you want this (so users can ",[33,1771,1772],{},"features = [\"serde_json\"]","), sometimes you don't.",[136,1775,1776,1781,1782,378],{},[339,1777,1778],{},[33,1779,1780],{},"cargo build --features \"\""," is sometimes needed to override ",[33,1783,1784],{},"default-features",[136,1786,1787,1792,1793,1796],{},[339,1788,1789,1791],{},[33,1790,761],{}," and feature interaction",": read ",[33,1794,1795],{},"CARGO_FEATURE_*"," env vars in build scripts.",[136,1798,1799,1802,1803,1805],{},[339,1800,1801],{},"Profile inheritance",": a custom profile that doesn't ",[33,1804,656],{}," from another starts empty (potentially wrong optimization).",[136,1807,1808,1812,1813,898,1815,1817],{},[339,1809,1810],{},[33,1811,745],{}," can be slower at runtime than ",[33,1814,749],{},[33,1816,753],{}," despite smaller binaries.",[18,1819,1821],{"id":1820},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1823,1824,1825,1827],{},"Two crates in the same dependency graph both use ",[33,1826,328],{},", with different feature needs. What actually happens at build time?",[23,1829,1830],{"language":25},[27,1831,1833],{"className":29,"code":1832,"language":25,"meta":31,"style":31},"# crate-a\u002FCargo.toml\n[dependencies]\nserde = { version = \"1\", default-features = false }\n\n# crate-b\u002FCargo.toml (also in the same build)\n[dependencies]\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\n",[33,1834,1835,1840,1848,1864,1868,1873,1881],{"__ignoreMap":31},[36,1836,1837],{"class":38,"line":39},[36,1838,1839],{"class":42},"# crate-a\u002FCargo.toml\n",[36,1841,1842,1844,1846],{"class":38,"line":46},[36,1843,50],{"class":49},[36,1845,171],{"class":53},[36,1847,57],{"class":49},[36,1849,1850,1853,1856,1859,1862],{"class":38,"line":60},[36,1851,1852],{"class":49},"serde = { version = ",[36,1854,1855],{"class":66},"\"1\"",[36,1857,1858],{"class":49},", default-features = ",[36,1860,1861],{"class":187},"false",[36,1863,191],{"class":49},[36,1865,1866],{"class":38,"line":78},[36,1867,243],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":242},[36,1869,1870],{"class":38,"line":93},[36,1871,1872],{"class":42},"# crate-b\u002FCargo.toml (also in the same build)\n",[36,1874,1875,1877,1879],{"class":38,"line":104},[36,1876,50],{"class":49},[36,1878,171],{"class":53},[36,1880,57],{"class":49},[36,1882,1883,1885,1887,1890,1893],{"class":38,"line":123},[36,1884,1852],{"class":49},[36,1886,1855],{"class":66},[36,1888,1889],{"class":49},", features = [",[36,1891,1892],{"class":66},"\"derive\"",[36,1894,1895],{"class":49},"] }\n",[1897,1898,1899,1903,1922,1972,1979],"details",{},[1900,1901,1902],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1904,1905,1907,1908,1910,1911,1914,1915,1918,1919,1921],{},[33,1906,328],{}," gets compiled with the ",[33,1909,332],{}," feature enabled for ",[339,1912,1913],{},"both"," crates — including ",[33,1916,1917],{},"crate-a",", which explicitly asked for ",[33,1920,351],{}," and no extra features.",[14,1923,1924,1925,1928,1929,1932,1933,1935,1936,1938,1939,1941,1942,1944,1945,1947,1948,1951,1952,1954,1955,1957,1958,1961,1962,70,1964,329,1966,1968,1969,1971],{},"Cargo's feature unification is graph-wide, not per-crate: within a single build (one ",[33,1926,1927],{},"Cargo.lock"," resolution), there is exactly ",[339,1930,1931],{},"one"," compiled version of ",[33,1934,328],{}," with ",[339,1937,1931],{}," feature set, and that set is the union of every feature requested by every crate that depends on it, anywhere in the graph. ",[33,1940,1917],{},"'s ",[33,1943,351],{}," only means \"don't turn on ",[33,1946,328],{},"'s own defaults ",[322,1949,1950],{},"from crate-a's request","\" — it does not mean \"guarantee ",[33,1953,328],{}," compiles without ",[33,1956,332],{}," no matter what else needs it.\" If ",[33,1959,1960],{},"crate-b"," (a sibling dependency, possibly many levels removed) asks for ",[33,1963,332],{},[33,1965,1917],{},[33,1967,332],{},"-enabled ",[33,1970,328],{}," too, silently, with no warning that its own more restrictive request was overridden by unification.",[14,1973,1974,1975,1978],{},"This is precisely why the \"Additive-Only Rule\" in this chapter matters: since you cannot reliably prevent a feature from being enabled by ",[322,1976,1977],{},"someone else"," in the graph, features must never change behavior in a way that would break a crate expecting them to be off — they can only ever add capability.",[14,1980,1981,1984,1985,1987],{},[339,1982,1983],{},"The lesson",": Cargo feature unification means a crate's ",[33,1986,351],{}," only affects its own request — if any other crate anywhere in the build graph requests a feature, everyone using that dependency gets it, with no per-crate opt-out.",[18,1989,1990],{"id":1900},"Summary",[14,1992,1993,1994,1558,1996,1998,1999,2001,2002,2004],{},"Features are additive conditional-compilation flags. Design them additive-only. Use ",[33,1995,197],{},[33,1997,1760],{}," for clean dep\u002Ffeature separation. Profiles control optimization and binary properties. ",[33,2000,761],{}," enables codegen and linking. CI should run fmt\u002Fclippy\u002Ftest\u002Fdoc and cross-compile. Use ",[33,2003,1112],{}," for versioning and publishing. Set and test the MSRV.",[14,2006,2007],{},"Next: The deeper type system — variance, HRTBs, and tricky generics.",[2009,2010,2011],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-defau